{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/762759-guidebook-to-stygia-chapter-3-5-the-doomslayers","id":762759,"title":"Guidebook to Stygia, Chapter 3.5, the Doomslayers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-10T19:15:38-08:00","id":762759,"title":"Guidebook to Stygia, Chapter 3.5, the Doomslayers","content":"&quot;Vermin who's time will end as the Malfeans wriggle out of the Labyrinth and march on the Necropoli to feast on the souls of the weak!- Blacktongue, Shade Caste Spectre.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I keep telling old Smiley that anybody who's willing to charge down into the Labyrinth with little more then a sword and a couple poached Dark Arcanoi clearly had SOME form of madness when they died, but so far my petitions fall on deaf ears.- The Laughing Lady&quot; <br /> <br /> This is a subchapter of my guidebook, you'll find them in here occasionally detailing aspects of Stygian life that don't QUITE fit in with the rest of the districts and the chapters detailing what's inside the walls of Stygia. Specifically, this covers the Stygian chapterhouse of the Doomslayers, those souls either brave enough, insane enough, or some combination of both to dive into the Labyrinth to beat the holy snot out of the Shadow Eaten. <br /> <br /> The exact means by which the Doomslayers where founded is shrouded in myth, mostly because literally anybody who considers themselves a Doomslayer essentially is one. The only real qualification is that you dive into the Labyrinth to hinder Spectres in some way. There's a few different categories of Doomslayers, ranging from the Thorns who are the &quot;First ones in, last ones out&quot; in any campaign against the Spectres, the Martyr Knights who primarily stay in Stygia and other Necropoli to watch out for signs of spectral infiltration (Some of the more recent Enfants have taken to calling them &quot;The Emperors Inquisition&quot; for some reason), the Helldivers who disguise themselves as Spectres for subversion and espionage, and a subsect of the Pardoners who follow the others along to make sure they do not become that which they hate most. <br /> <br /> There are also individual Doomslayers who don't belong to any of these groups, who usually are in it for Charons Bounty. Around the time of the Fifth Great Malestrom, Charon put a bounty on spectral corpses, if you brought back a chunk of their Corpus, you'd be paid for your trouble. Naturally this lead to an entire generation of new Doomslayers hunting Spectres to make a quick Obulus. <br /> <br /> <br /> Doomslayer Chapterhouse: Stygian Branch<br /> <br /> Built right next to the Commandery of the Martyr Knights, the Grand Chapterhouse is a place where Doomslayers meet to report their findings in the Labyrinth to those who work directly with the Five, the enigmatic leaders of the Doomslayers. Due to their paranoia, exceedingly few Wraiths have any idea who leads the Doomslayers, only that there's five of them and that pondering too much on their nature tends to lead to...problems. <br /> <br /> The Chapterhouse doubles as a recruitment center, training hall, dojo, and library on spectral lore. Anything that's up to date and covers recent events in the Labyrinth cannot be found here, however. But if you want to sign up to fight Spectres, learn how to kill them, or try and hire one out for a specific mission (Don't try this with anybody who isn't independent, the more professional ones generally consider private jobs a distraction) <br /> <br /> Physically, the Chapterhouse resembles an old European hunting lodge, the kind of place where noblemen would hang taxidermied animals they've shot, and retire after a long day of chasing foxes on horseback. However, its far grander in size, dwarfing most mansions in the Skinlands, and covered in soulforged plaques detailing what Spectre the soulsteel is made of, how it was brought down, and who did the killing. <br /> <br /> Most Doomslayers don't particularly care for grandiose displays, but its not for them. The point of the Chapterhouse is, primarily, to obtain new recruits, and remind Stygia that the Doomslayers are vital to the survival of the Dark Kingdom of Iron and the Shadowlands proper. It draws Enfants in with tales of glory and coin to be made, while assuming anybody who's survived long enough to matter in the Doomslayers generally doesn't care about much more then hunting down the next batch of Mortwights. <br /> <br /> <br /> Who would be mad enough...<br /> <br /> With the recent wars in the Skinlands, though not as large as the World Wars, the population of Wraiths in the Middle East has expanded considerably. As ISIS terrorists fight Syrians and pretty much everybody else, as Iraq is overrun by partisans, and as Syria fights a bloody civil war, people are dying with great amounts of passion and unfinished business. While the Spectre population in these areas has risen considerably thanks to the atrocities of ISIS (Or ISIL or whatever they're calling themselves this week), leading to Mortwights born of people who where set on fire as the video was recorded to end up on Al Jazeera, Striplings born of murdered children and raped girls, and plenty of Shades who liked the raping, murder and pillage so much they just kept on doing it in the Shadowlands even as they grew shark teeth and claws. <br /> <br /> But the thing is, for every tormented soul, or soul who enjoys torment who falls to their Shadow, there's someone dying on the battlefield who's not ready to give up the fight. They want their homeland back, they want ISIS out, they want safety and they're not afraid to fight for it. The Doomslayers are having something of a renaissance, soldiers from the Iraq war, young men and women who fought for freedom in the Arab Spring, Syrian resistance fighters, and many more are crossing the shroud, realizing there's still a war going on...and picking up their relics to bring the fight to the Spectres. <br /> <br /> Due to the chaos, the Dictum Mortuum is not heavily enforced in this area, and the shroud tends to be particularly low in these regions (Some mystics mention a Web of Faith throughout the middle east, put in place by ancient magicians, but I've heard little more then second or third hand accounts of this). More then a few Soldiers have simply stayed in the Shadowlands long enough to learn some Embody and drop back to the other side, taking advantage of how generally difficult they are to 'kill' to keep the fight going, using the Fog to their advantage as they cut down more of their enemies. <br /> <br /> Word is the Puppeteers Guild, banished from Stygia, is in the area as well, training Wraiths to possess their old bodies and carry on as the legendary Risen. Revenants who exist in the Skinlands as undead, who tend to be some of the most obsessed Wraiths you'll ever see. You can imagine how terrified an ISIS terrorist would be upon emptying an entire clip into a dead man and still having him continue the fight without so much as a flinch. Adding to the good news, Spectres can rarely influence the Skinlands with any degree of success due to their dark nature, the mechanics are still not very well understood, but it IS known they lack Lifesight, and generally cannot peek in on goings on in the land of the living. <br /> <br /> However, all the chaos in the area, while not sufficient to, as far as we know, cause a Great Maelstrom, it HAS caused lesser Maelstroms to rise from the Tempest. This only adds to the chaos of the region, which is quickly reaching the point where Ferrymen have been spotted in the area trying to bring things back under control. Furthermore, some Hierarchy officials have been petitioning to send entire legions of soldiers into that portion of the Shadowlands in order to forcibly subdue and end the fighting. <br /> <br /> But that would simply be a bandage, as long has the Middle East continues to be a war zone, there won't be lasting peace in the Shadowlands. This humble author simply hopes that those who carry on the crusade against the Shadow-Eaten can endure long enough until the Quick get their act together. But it is a fragile hope indeed...<br /> <br /> <br /> Authors Notes<br /> <br /> The intent here was to give a brief Shoah like-look at the consequences the unrest in the Middle East has had on the Shadowlands. I salute those soldiers who enlisted to help fight the barbarism of these would-be tyrants and those rebels who fight for freedom and their homeland, and wish them nothing but success and a quick victory against ISIS and other terrorist groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1645-autochthon","name":"Autochthon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}